  GATE 2 (solution): R1 = does this actually resolve the pain, or is it a feature nobody switches for? · R2 = incumbent response — why won't a funded incumbent just do this / where is the durable edge? · R3 = what's the load-bearing assumption the whole concept dies to, and can the proposed test actually de-risk it?
  GATE 3 (business): R1 = distribution — how does it REACH the buyer, concretely? · R2 = unit economics — does revenue clear CAC + cost-to-serve? · R3 = the path (OSS-first / wedge / services-led) — is the sequencing real or hand-waved, and what's the compounding advantage?

